RESUME SKILL GAP ANALYZER - HTML Implementation Documentation
================================================================

1. IMPLEMENTATION OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Created 4 separate HTML files with consistent styling and sidebar navigation:

Files Created:
- login.html - User authentication
- register.html - Account creation  
- dashboard.html - Resume upload and role selection
- result.html - Analysis results display

Architecture:
- Multiple page approach (separate HTML files)
- Sidebar layout navigation
- Glassmorphism + Bold UI styling
- Medium animation level


2. FILE STRUCTURES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

LOGIN.HTML
├── Sidebar Navigation
│   ├── Logo
│   ├── Nav Items (Login, Register)
│   └── User Info
└── Main Content
    ├── Auth Card
    ├── Login Form (email, password)
    └── Register Link

REGISTER.HTML
├── Sidebar Navigation
│   ├── Logo
│   ├── Nav Items (Login, Register)
│   └── User Info
└── Main Content
    ├── Auth Card
    ├── Register Form (name, email, password)
    └── Login Link

DASHBOARD.HTML
├── Sidebar Navigation
│   ├── Logo
│   ├── Nav Items (Dashboard, History, Settings)
│   └── Logout Button
└── Main Content
    ├── Page Header
    ├── Dashboard Grid (2 columns)
    │   ├── Upload Card (drag-drop)
    │   └── Role Selection Card
    │       ├── Category Dropdown (14 categories)
    │       ├── Skills Grid
    │       └── Analyze Button

RESULT.HTML
├── Sidebar Navigation
│   ├── Logo
│   ├── Nav Items (Dashboard, Results, Settings)
│   └── Logout Button
└── Main Content
    ├── Result Header
    ├── Score Section (circular visualization)
    ├── Progress Grid (4 categories)
    ├── Recommendations Grid (3 cards)
    └── Action Buttons


3. JOB CATEGORIES (14 Total)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Software Development
2. Web Development
3. Mobile Development
4. UI/UX Design
5. Data Science
6. AI/ML
7. Cloud Computing
8. Cybersecurity
9. Database Engineering
10. DevOps
11. Networking
12. Game Development
13. QA/Testing
14. Project Management

Each category has 10 associated skills stored in JavaScript object.


4. COMPONENTS IMPLEMENTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input Components:
- Text inputs with focus effects
- Password inputs
- Email inputs
- File upload input (hidden, triggered by click)

Select Components:
- Category dropdown with custom styling
- 14 options with icons

Display Components:
- Circular score visualization (CSS conic-gradient)
- Progress bars (4 categories)
- Skill tags (selectable)
- Recommendation cards (3)

Button Components:
- Primary buttons (gradient background)
- Outline buttons (border styling)
- Upload area (drag-drop zone)


5. STYLING DECISIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Color Theme (Neon):
- Background: #0a0a0f (dark)
- Glass background: rgba(21, 21, 31, 0.7)
- Neon Cyan: #00f5ff (primary)
- Neon Purple: #bf00ff (accent)
- Neon Pink: #ff00a8 (secondary)
- Neon Green: #00ff88 (success)
- Neon Blue: #0080ff (info)
- Neon Orange: #ff6b00 (warning)

UI Style (Glassmorphism + Bold):
- backdrop-filter: blur(20px)
- Glass borders with transparency
- Bold typography (Inter font)
- Large touch targets
- Defined shadows and glows

Animation Level (Medium):
- Page transitions (fadeIn, slideUp)
- Button hover effects
- Upload area animations
- Progress bar fill animations
- Score circle rotation
- Shimmer effect on progress bars
- Card hover lift effects


6. LAYOUT STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sidebar (280px fixed):
- Logo section
- Navigation links
- User info / Logout

Main Content (flex: 1):
- Responsive grid system
- Card-based components
- Maximum width constraints

Responsive Breakpoints:
- Desktop: > 1024px
- Tablet: 768px - 1024px
- Mobile: < 768px (sidebar hidden)


7. JAVASCRIPT FUNCTIONALITY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Dashboard Page:
- File upload handling
- Drag-and-drop support
- File validation (PDF/DOCX, 5MB max)
- Category selection
- Dynamic skills loading
- Form validation

Pages Navigation:
- Simple href navigation between pages
- Form submission handlers redirecting to next page


8. ASSUMPTIONS MADE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. No backend integration (static demo)
2. Single session (no auth persistence)
3. Browser-based only
4. Modern browser support (CSS3, ES6)
5. Static skill data
6. Sample score results


9. HOW TO USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Open login.html in browser
2. Click "Register" to create account
3. Fill form and submit
4. On dashboard, upload resume file
5. Select job category from dropdown
6. Click skills to select/deselect
7. Click "Analyze Resume"
8. View results on result page
9. Click "New Analysis" to start over


10. FILE DETAILS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Each HTML file includes:
- Complete <head> with meta tags
- Google Fonts (Inter)
- Internal CSS styles
- HTML structure
- Inline JavaScript

No external dependencies except Google Fonts CDN.


